  "notes": "# Rove 0.1.15\n\n- Review preserved local sessions from 0.1.13 and recovery copies kept by\n  0.1.14, including unsaved new Requests, edited saved Requests, Suites, Folders,\n  Environments and Variables. Draft and saved versions remain separate.\n- Choose the matching workspace explicitly before continuing. Recovery review\n  stays on this device and does not execute Requests, Scripts or Schedules.\n  Schedules remain paused after association until explicitly resumed; Scripts\n  still require workspace trust.\n- Keep immutable recovery copies before association and refuse stale or\n  conflicting recovery writes. Reopening a completed recovery preserves later\n  edits rather than replaying the old copy over them.\n- Reload workspace files after reopening only when the empty cache is proven\n  to follow a successfully preserved recovery. Unknown ownership and malformed\n  recovery data remain available for review or download.\n\nClose other Rove windows, including older versions, before associating recovered\nwork. This recovery route supports one participating editor; it does not promise\natomic coordination with older versions that write Environment storage directly.\n\nThis release targets macOS arm64 through the existing beta update channel.\nThe signed minimum stays at 0.1.13. Existing Windows and legacy download assets\nretain their versions. macOS platform signing remains ad hoc, without Apple\nnotarization.\n",
